// @run
// @log 1
// @log 7
// The `Circle[]` annotation is DECLARED redundant rather than deleted: it is the kind-1
// destination, i.e. the whole subject of this fixture. Removing it removes the defect.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `cS` is inferred as `{r: i32}[]`
// TWO BINDINGS THAT ONLY SHARE A NAME ARE NOT ONE BINDING WITH TWO DESTINATIONS (D661).
//
// Each `lv1` below has exactly ONE declared destination. `fu`'s is the union-box list
// `Shape[]`, `fs`'s is the plain struct-row list `Circle[]`, and neither function can see
// the other's local. Both are D381's own subject, standing alone, and each RUNS when it is
// the only thing in the file.
//
// Together they were a positioned emit reject on master — D411's "one un-annotated list
// literal is bound to TWO declared destinations whose elements are stored differently" —
// because `letRefListDestSlotK`'s destination scan was `while i < P.nodes.length` over the
// WHOLE arena, matched on the binding's NAME. The header said so ("NAME-SCOPED OVER THE
// WHOLE ARENA"); what it did not say is that a name is not a binding. Renaming `fs`'s
// `lv1` to `lv2` was the only edit needed to make this same program run.
//
// The fix is the binding's own SCOPE: `fnIx`'s body once `parentLetOf` confirms this
// binding is what the name denotes there, the module root for a global, and the
// whole-arena scan kept unchanged where neither confirms — a binding whose scope cannot
// be named is one whose destinations a scoped walk could silently MISS, and a missed
// destination is D381 un-landing into a check-clean invalid module.
//
// Measured on `scripts/silent-sweep/d661/`: 172 of 211 cells `loud emit reject` -> `runs`,
// 0 `runs` lost, 0 into any silent class, and D411's own 103-cell grid is UNMOVED (96
// still refused, all 7 single-destination controls still running). The two-destination
// refusal is a design rule about ONE list value and it is untouched here; what moved is
// which bindings count as one.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
function fu() {
  const lv1 = [{ r: 7 }]
  const cU: Shape[] = lv1
  if cU.length > 0 { print(cU.length) } else { print(0) }
}
function fs() {
  const lv1 = [{ r: 7 }]
  const cS: Circle[] = lv1
  if cS.length > 0 { print(cS[0].r) } else { print(0) }
}
fu()
fs()
